{
 "format": "mainaiger",
 "schema_version": 2,
 "notebook": {
  "nbformat": 4,
  "nbformat_minor": 5,
  "metadata": {
   "kernelspec": {
    "name": "python3",
    "display_name": "Python 3",
    "language": "python"
   },
   "mainaiger": {
    "example": true,
    "name": "ask-memory",
    "title": "Ask memory as a Mainbook (search, choose, ask, keep)"
   }
  },
  "cells": [
   {
    "id": "readme",
    "cell_type": "markdown",
    "metadata": {
     "mainaiger": {
      "title": "Ask memory, as a Mainbook"
     }
    },
    "source": "# Ask memory, as a Mainbook\n\nThe same three stages as the ASK box on the Memory page, laid out as cards so you can change the rule in the middle. **Question** is a form; **Search memory** is a Memory cell (the Lab searches your notes on this Mac and stores `hits`); **Choose notes** is ordinary Python — it decides which hits to hand to the model (edit it: prefer stable notes, require a title match, cap the count, or stop the run with `raise SystemExit` when a stable note already answers); **Ask with notes** is a Memory cell that asks your local model with those notes and stores `answer`; **Keep the answer** writes it as a draft note; **Report** prints it. Needs a running session, an approved Memory folder and an installed model.\n",
    "outputs": []
   },
   {
    "id": "question",
    "cell_type": "code",
    "metadata": {
     "mainaiger": {
      "title": "Question",
      "form": {
       "fields": [
        {
         "name": "question",
         "type": "text",
         "label": "Your question",
         "default": "What do I know about this project?"
        }
       ],
       "values": {}
      }
     }
    },
    "source": "print(\"asking:\", question)\n",
    "execution_count": null,
    "outputs": []
   },
   {
    "id": "search",
    "cell_type": "code",
    "metadata": {
     "mainaiger": {
      "title": "Search memory",
      "memory": {
       "op": "search",
       "output": "hits"
      }
     }
    },
    "source": "",
    "execution_count": null,
    "outputs": []
   },
   {
    "id": "choose",
    "cell_type": "code",
    "metadata": {
     "mainaiger": {
      "title": "Choose notes"
     }
    },
    "source": "# The rule for what memory the model may see. Edit freely; it is plain Python over `hits`.\nstable = [h for h in hits if h[\"status\"] == \"stable\"]\nchosen = (stable or hits)[:3]\nuse = [h[\"path\"] for h in chosen]\nprint(\"question:\", question)\nprint(\"%d hit(s); using %d:\" % (len(hits), len(use)))\nfor h in chosen:\n    print(\" -\", h[\"title\"], \"(%s)\" % h[\"status\"])\nif not hits:\n    print(\"nothing in memory matches; the model answers from scratch\")\n",
    "execution_count": null,
    "outputs": []
   },
   {
    "id": "ask",
    "cell_type": "code",
    "metadata": {
     "mainaiger": {
      "title": "Ask with notes",
      "memory": {
       "op": "ask",
       "output": "answer"
      }
     }
    },
    "source": "",
    "execution_count": null,
    "outputs": []
   },
   {
    "id": "keep",
    "cell_type": "code",
    "metadata": {
     "mainaiger": {
      "title": "Keep the answer"
     }
    },
    "source": "title = \"Q: \" + question[:70]\nbody = answer[\"reply\"] + \"\\n\\n## Question\\n\\n\" + question + (\"\\n\\n## Notes used\\n\\n\" + \"\\n\".join(\"- \" + p for p in answer[\"used\"]) if answer[\"used\"] else \"\")\nkind = \"answer\"\ntags = [\"ask\", \"mainbook\"]\nprint(\"writing a draft answer note…\")\n",
    "execution_count": null,
    "outputs": []
   },
   {
    "id": "write",
    "cell_type": "code",
    "metadata": {
     "mainaiger": {
      "title": "Write the note",
      "memory": {
       "op": "write",
       "output": "note_path"
      }
     }
    },
    "source": "",
    "execution_count": null,
    "outputs": []
   },
   {
    "id": "report",
    "cell_type": "code",
    "metadata": {
     "mainaiger": {
      "title": "Report"
     }
    },
    "source": "print(\"=\" * 48)\nprint(answer[\"reply\"].strip())\nprint(\"=\" * 48)\nprint(\"model:\", answer[\"model\"], \"| %d ms\" % answer[\"elapsed_ms\"], \"| notes used:\", len(answer[\"used\"]), \"| saved as:\", note_path)\n",
    "execution_count": null,
    "outputs": []
   }
  ]
 },
